   415	## 7. FG composition
   416	
   417	### 7.1 Decisions (user, 2026-09-28)
   418	
   419	- The FG is fixed. `Kit.FG` is our Simplex FG (the DC §7 finality gadget,
   420	  without SG, grades or safe votes) as one verified module. It is not a
   421	  catalog variable. Its lemmas (§7.4) are proved once.
   422	- Available protocols (APs) vary. An AP plugs in by proving the AP-side
   423	  entries (§7.3). The composite claims then follow from `Kit.Compose`
   424	  (§7.5) with no composite-specific proof.
   425	- FG heights never skip: a block's state height is its parent's or one
   426	  more.
   427	- Every height pair, a target and also a timeout, needs a certified
   428	  source (the AP's `FGTarget`); with no source the pair is empty. This is
   429	  a rule of the fixed module (the user's decision "timeouts need a
   430	  confirmation too; one C_fg").
   431	- History: r94 showed that a naive FG on SA breaks SA's P1. The current
   432	  FG-SA rule set uses a self-certifying source and is consistent with
   433	  this interface (Opus paper check, fgsa-fast-opus.md; Astra r143 and the
   434	  r146 adjudication are still open on parts).
   435	- Fallback: an AP that cannot meet the AP-side entries is certified
   436	  white-box as one composite instance.
   437	
   438	### 7.2 Interface
   439	
   440	**FG → AP: a fixed anchor function of a view.**
   441	
   442	`anchorsOf : View → Block × Finset Block` returns `(F, anchors)` for a
   443	block view. It is part of `Kit.FG` and does not vary.
   444	
   445	- It is evaluated at DUTY time on the duty's own view (the frozen HEAD
   446	  view, the full proposal view), not on the live store. A late witness in
   447	  the live store must not raise the band in a frozen view that does not
   448	  contain it (R1; r125 §4).
   449	- Every duty view contains the evidence basis of the current F (its
   450	  accepting carrier, its J carrier, and a descendant witness; r143 §2.1).
   451	  Without it F can be non-viable in a frozen view.
   452	- `anchors` = the viable entries at FG height h_max − 1 above the FG root:
   453	  blocks B with σ[B].h = h_max − 1 and σ[B.parent].h < h_max − 1.
   454	  Because heights never skip, each viable branch passes exactly one such
   455	  entry, so the set is a finite antichain. When the root is J
   456	  (h_max = h_j + 1), J is the entry of height h_j and anchors = {J}.
   457	  At the start, anchors = {genesis}. This set gives the same blocks as
   458	  DC's viable set (checked by the async session, round 3).
   459	- `process` does only FG admission (F ⪯ B) for the choice tree. Finality
   460	  is processed live in DC order (finality first, then height).
   461	
   462	**AP → FG: facets.**
   463	
   464	- `FGTarget`: the AP's target at the FG action, read through the base
   465	  projection. The FG uses it as the height-pair source; if it is empty,
   466	  the pair is empty.
   467	- `AnchorChoice`: the AP's rule to pick one anchor from `anchorsOf` of a
   468	  duty view. Only the HEAD and proposal walks read anchors. Other AP
   469	  rules (FG-SA's release, confirmation and lease-write gates) may run on
   470	  the unfiltered raw tree. DC's rule is the greedy walk from the root
   471	  without a majority gate below the band; FG-SA can pick the anchor that
   472	  extends its Protected lease.
   473	- FG attestations travel as block payload (the FG proposer is the block
   474	  proposer; §11 Q1).
   475	
   476	- `FinalityHead`: the AP head at the FG action. The DC finality pair
   477	  comes from it, not from `FGTarget` (r143 §3.3).
   478	- Row inclusion: honest proposals carry the FG rows they received (see
   479	  `ap.includesRows`).
   480	
   481	**Standalone form (no engine input).** AP-side entries are proved for
   482	`AP ⊗ HavocFG`. HavocFG fixes the FG state transition (heights, entries,
   483	J and F processing), admission, the anchor function and the payload
   484	format. Only the honest FG signing rule varies: it is a universally
   485	quantified parameter, and it may make honest FG signers equivocate. That
   486	is harmless for the AP claims; the FG-internal claims (accountable
   487	safety, honest never slashable) stay in `Kit.FG` with the durable Λ.
   488	`Kit.Compose` instantiates the parameter with the Simplex FG signing rule.
   489	This replaces the v3 run-input proposal (E7): a parametric composite
   490	needs no engine change.
   491	
   492	### 7.3 AP-side entries
   493	
   494	Conditions on runs of `AP ⊗ HavocFG` (L1):
   495	
   496	The conditions mention only ANCHOR VALUES at honest duties and the AP's
   497	own `FGTarget` history, never FG objects. So they are observable in
   498	`AP ⊗ HavocFG`, and AP proofs never need to know why the anchors changed.
   499	Provenance statements belong only to the FG side (§7.4 (C)).
   500	
   501	- `Static [t₀, t₁)`: at every honest duty in the interval, after the
   502	  settling time, `anchorsOf` of the duty view and F are constant, except
   503	  for changes whose new anchor set contains an anchor compatible with
   504	  every honest `FGTarget` read at or after t₀.
   505	- `TargetPreserving u`: no honest duty's anchor set excludes a block that
   506	  was an honest node's `FGTarget` at a duty at or after u.
   507	- `ProtectedCompatible` (only for the clean and Outage regimes, where the
   508	  honest Protected blocks lie on one chain): every honest anchor set
   509	  contains an anchor compatible with every honest Protected block. It is
   510	  an explicit premise of the AP claims under HavocFG: havoc honest votes
   511	  can form any quorum, so it is not implied.
   512	
   513	```text
   514	┌──────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   515	│ Entry                │ Statement                                      │
   516	├──────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
   517	│ ap.floored           │ F ⪯ every AP output at every honest read       │
   518	│ ap.anchorCompliant   │ the head, the finality head and the target     │
   519	│                      │ descend the chosen anchor (needed for height   │
   520	│                      │ progress)                                      │
   521	│ ap.includesRows      │ every honest proposal includes every FG row    │
