  1993	The vote duty uses a block-domain merge analogous to its vote merge.
  1994	It first forms a processed-block view from blocks received before the
  1995	previous-slot freeze and every ancestor of a current-slot proposal, then
  1996	recomputes viability and the filtered block tree inside that view.  In
  1997	particular, it does not filter the current viable tree after the fact: a
  1998	late witness cannot make an old pre-freeze child enter this vote's walk.
  1999	The proposer and the other protocol duties keep the ordinary full-tree
  2000	$\Call{get\_head}{}$.
