   293	**Lease priority is a proof obligation at every path to an output.**
   294	
   295	The following is the required design discipline, not a theorem for an
   296	already implemented full protocol.
   297	
   298	```text
   299	┌──────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┐
   300	│ State                        │ Required treatment                    │
   301	├──────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┤
   302	│ F, J, lease R are comparable │ Keep the deepest required prefix.     │
   303	│ J conflicts with live R      │ Retain J's proof; keep R mandatory;   │
   304	│                              │ omit an incompatible FG target vote.  │
   305	│ Φ conflicts with live R      │ R wins. The floor cannot release R.   │
   306	│ Φ is an ancestor of PC C     │ Retain C if the FG domain admits it.  │
   307	│ Φ conflicts with C           │ Use F4 inside the admitted domain.    │
   308	│ New J arrives after freeze   │ Archive it; defer its epoch-root use. │
   309	│ Finality proof conflicts R/S │ Retain the proof; do not erase R or   │
   310	│                              │ silently replace S. Repair is needed. │
   311	│ New S or lease write         │ Apply its own guards at the gate.     │
   312	└──────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────┘
   313	```
   314	
   315	There is no total priority order “F, then J, then leases, then F4” that
   316	solves an arbitrary inconsistent state. A domain restriction can bypass a
   317	lease before the root comparison runs. Conversely, an eternal lease veto
   318	can cause E2. The protocol needs a bounded way to make these constraints
   319	compatible. A sound joint invariant must also show that a conflicting
   320	finality certificate cannot require removal of an armed base prefix within
   321	its promised regime. Until that is proved, do not infer safety from the
   322	accessor identity finalized⪯available.
   323	
   324	The pending gate is part of that invariant. SA's general P1 does not assume
   325	that every reader has a protecting lease at outage onset. The last healthy
   326	batch can first write that lease after b₀. SA-PC therefore saves the whole
   327	raw genuine result, guards S separately, and evaluates each ancestor's own
   328	lease admission and PC compatibility. The red-team execution with
   329	n=16, a=6, h=7, τ=8, q=11, k=4, L=15 has a PC(C) that vetoes a raw D tip
   330	below the protected common ancestor B. Its gate at 26 must still write
   331	E(B)=41. The literal whole-gate veto loses B at 34, before b₁=37.25.
   332	[Exact boundary execution](sapc-redteam.md)
   333	
   334	An FG guard must preserve this prefix loop. “The raw tip conflicts with J,
   335	therefore skip the gate” is not a valid port. Nor is the invariant that
   336	every lease target is a prefix of S: red-team execution M refutes it.
   337	Use the actual raw-result source, admission test, guards, and deadline.
   338	
   339	**The r19 freeze remains useful, but its transfer premise changes.**
   340	
   341	The freeze and opening-proposer merge address late FG evidence. A clock
   342	deadline alone does not give common evidence: a faulty certificate can
   343	reach one reader just before the deadline and another just after it. R19's
   344	proposer carries the maximum justified source and the proof dependencies.
   345	Under relay, an honest proposer dominates every honest frozen choice.
